# 060 — UI Rules: Blazor Server + MudBlazor

## Framework

- **Blazor Server** (not Blazor WebAssembly).
- **MudBlazor** as the component library. No Bootstrap, no MUI-React equivalent.
- SignalR-driven interactivity built into Blazor Server.
- Server-side rendering — UI state lives on the server.

## Why Not React or Other SPA

This decision is final. See `docs/adr/ADR-0001-technology-stack.md` and `docs/adr/ADR-0007-iis-hosting-model.md`.

Reasons (do not re-litigate):
- Single .NET ecosystem reduces context-switching cost for the single developer.
- Native Windows Authentication integration without custom token handling.
- No SPA build pipeline, no npm dependency hell.
- MudBlazor provides a complete component set out of the box.

